== 2. Pre-registration, verbatim ==
PRE-REGISTRATION: where layer overlap's gain comes from, traced, YOLOv8s. Desktop 2 (DESKTOP-CBL5NUA), 2026-10-15.
Written before any traced dispatch of the overlap build. Disclosed: the decomposition script was dry-run on the
control-only tail-sitting JSONs (ctl against itself: control gaps 6,256,428 cycles, within-layer 21,441,406).

Question. --overlap-layers gained -1.220 ms real and -0.454 ms NOP (warm, edbb8b5), outside its prediction, with
real gaining 2.7x NOP. Does the gain come from the activation stream's idle gaps between layers, or from inside
layers?

Containers: build/yolov8s_tr_ctl.ignite and its NOP copy (as before); build/yolov8s_tr_ov.ignite (= --overlap-layers
--trace-shims 0) and its NOP copy (write_nop_copy). Hashes below. Exactness of tr_ov is checked in this sitting's
log before the timing rounds (repeat_dispatch_exact --iters 20 against yolov8s_ab_ctl's heads); a failure voids it.

Method. scratch/b48/sit4.py --rounds 6 (ctl, ov, ctl_nop, ov_nop rotated; one cold traced dispatch per process)
under research-lowlevel.sh --npu; void unless timing_eligible true. Then scratch/b48/decompose.py: from the
per-layer activation completion offsets, the frame = head + sum(within-layer first-to-last completion spans) +
sum(gaps between layer k's last and k+1's first completion) + end. Note: under overlap a layer's marker fires when
it starts issuing, so the decomposition uses absolute completion times, not windows.

Gates: C, the traced frame gain within 0.40 ms of the warm -1.220 (real) and within 0.30 ms of -0.454 (NOP). If C
fails for an arm, that arm's V is reported but not read as the warm mechanism.

Rule V (per arm, on the frame gain dF = ctl - ov): BOUNDARY when the gaps' share of dF >= 60%; WITHIN when the
within-layer share >= 60%; else MIXED.
Expectations (weak): real BOUNDARY or MIXED; NOP BOUNDARY. If real is BOUNDARY with a gap gain much larger than
NOP's, the asymmetry is that real frames' boundary gaps held compute-paced waiting the overlap removes. If real is
WITHIN or MIXED, the overlap changes inside-layer behaviour (e.g. issue off the critical path) and the section says
which groups carry it. Reported, not verdict-bearing: per compute-share group, gaps and within changes.

A hang, an exactness failure or contention voids the sitting.

== 3. Amendment after the first sitting, verbatim ==
AMENDMENT to scratch/b48/prereg_explain.txt (sha256 b204957a...), written 2026-10-15 after the first sitting
(results/aie/overlap_explain_yolov8s_desktop2_20261015T2120Z.log) and before a second one.

What was seen from the first sitting, disclosed in full:
- Exactness PASS (20 dispatches each, heads equal to yolov8s_ab_ctl's).
- Gate C, both arms PASS: traced frame gain -1.171 ms real (warm -1.220), -0.422 ms NOP (warm -0.454).
- Rule V could not be computed. The overlap arms' per-window JSON has layers with no activation completion inside
  their own marker window (under overlap a marker fires when the layer starts issuing, so its completions can fall
  in the next window). The pre-registered decompose.py reads those as NaN: head, within and gaps are NaN for ov and
  ov_nop. One partial figure was printed and is disclosed: hi-group within change -1,268,620 cycles (real), from the
  layers whose windows did hold completions. No gap or within share was seen for either arm.

Amended method (V and C unchanged otherwise): attribute activation completions to layers BY COUNT, not by window.
Column 0's MM2S_0 completes its tasks in order and its FINISHED_TASK pulses are exact (1,387 per frame); the k-th
pulse belongs to the layer owning column 0's k-th activation task (a_tasks per layer from
shim_trace_budget_yolov8s_desktop2_20261015T1922Z.json). Script: scratch/b48/decompose2.py, which needs the raw
trace bytes, so a second sitting saves them (sit4.py now passes --dump-bytes; nothing else changed). It was
dry-run on three control dumps from the tail sitting (ctl against itself): within 21,364,095, gaps 6,256,851
cycles, agreeing with the window method's 21,441,406 and 6,256,428 where windows are valid.

The verdict is read from the SECOND sitting only, with its own gate C (same tolerances). The first sitting's
frame gains are reported beside it, not pooled.

